# Rasterizer — SDL2 software rasterizer (C++20, CMake + vcpkg)
#
# Scoped deliberately to three things: build output, restorable
# dependencies, and machine-local editor state. Everything else is tracked.

# ---- Build output ----
# VS's CMake integration configures into out/; build/ covers CLI builds.
[Oo]ut/
[Bb]uild/

# In-source CMake configure (easy to trigger by accident)
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake

# ---- Dependencies ----
# Restored from vcpkg.json + vcpkg-configuration.json on first configure.
# ~200 MB of SDL2 sources and build trees — never commit this.
vcpkg_installed/

# ---- Visual Studio local state ----
# Entirely machine-local. launch.vs.json deliberately lives at the repo root
# instead of in here, so it stays tracked: it records the debugger's working
# directory (${workspaceRoot}), which is what lets the program find its
# assets at runtime. VS reads it from the root just fine.
.vs/

# VS per-user settings
*.rsuser
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache

# ---- Compiler / debugger artifacts ----
# These normally land inside out/, but are listed to catch stray in-source builds.
#
# DELIBERATELY ABSENT: *.obj. In a C++ gitignore that means MSVC object files,
# but this project's geometry (cube.obj, teapot.obj) are Wavefront OBJ models.
# A blanket *.obj rule silently excludes the assets the renderer needs.
# Real object files already live under out/ and build/ above.
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.idb
*.pch
*.exp
*.exe
*.lib
*.dll

# ---- Editor / tooling ----
# Machine-local only; a shared .claude/settings.json would still be tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json

# ---- OS cruft ----
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
